From b1d8a3b8d0b44e53e9cfd2352420ac76de1e992e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 07:56:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Name the guided scene prompt so a second format can exist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The guided-story visual prompt was an unnamed template literal inside
guidedStoryStoryboard's scene map. Every guided video ever rendered went
through it, and nothing could call it or test it.

Seedance 2.5 needs a different prompt shape — a documented bracket
notation where the bracket is the meaning, and spoken lines carried in
the prompt because it generates audio with the picture. A format branch
cannot be added safely to an expression with no name and no coverage, so
this extracts first and branches later.

- guidedScenePrompt.ts: guidedSceneVisualPrompt(), the existing format
  moved out unchanged. Its test reproduces the pre-extraction literal
  character for character and asserts equality across the matrix that
  actually varies — backdrop label, location mode, logo, cast size,
  missing references — including the trailing blank lines a scene with no
  logo has always emitted. Those stay: tidying them would change the
  bytes of a prompt already known to work.

- seedancePrompt.ts: the Seedance assembly, landed but NOT wired. It is
  reviewable against the documented syntax before anything renders with
  it. Two slots per role, because a KOKAO character is two images — the
  reference whose face-and-hair rect is protected, and the outfit image
  where everything below is repainted. Story time is rebased onto clip
  time. Dialogue is numbered once across the whole script, keyed by line
  id so the numbering survives the coverage split. Only the five
  permitted negatives are emitted.

Rules that shape what the script WRITER invents are deliberately absent:
those belong in the governed guided_story_script prompt, because they
have to reach the model that writes the script. Only assembly is here.

Recorded in seedancePrompt.ts and not yet solved: scene.visual is baked
at storyboard time, before the video model is resolved, and
scene.inputFingerprint does not cover it. Two scenes built in different
formats hash identically, so the format has to enter that fingerprint
before any switch — otherwise a format change silently reuses previews
rendered under the old one.

Tests: 63 new, all passing. api-server videoGen suite unchanged at the
same two known failures (wallet shortfall, real-ffmpeg narration/music),
verified by running them against a stashed tree.

